#!grafli v4
# Do reloading and saving a board take the same steps? — a mirror
# Worked example of the mirror encoding (skill: references/design.md
# "Mirror"): reload on the left, save on the right, the board file on top,
# the canvas below, the same step at the same height on both sides. The
# step only one side has leaves a gap on the other. Left out, to keep to the
# board file's own text: doc bodies, which travel to and from the vault the
# same way (load_docs / save_docs), and the move of inline md: notes into
# the vault, which a save does once per note.
# source: ..

# ── claim ──
@ note claim 0,-260 "Reload and save meet in the same merge — only saving adds a step" ~xlarge !flat !sans !bold
@ note channel 0,-195 "mirror: left = an outside write is reloaded, right = autosave; the same step sits at the same height, and the step reload lacks leaves a gap" ~small !flat !sans

# ── sides ──
@ note h_reload 0,-110 "reload" ~large !flat !sans
@ note h_save 760,-110 "save" ~large !flat !sans

# ── shared ──
@ box file "board.grafli on disk" 380,-60 260x80
@ box canvas "Board in the canvas" 380,680 260x80

# ── reload ──
@ box parse "parse()" 0,280 260x80
@ box merge_r "merge_boards()" 0,480 260x80

# ── save ──
@ box swap "atomic_write()\ntemp file, then replace" 760,80 260x80 %accent !ink !bold
@ box serialize "serialize()" 760,280 260x80
@ box merge_w "merge_boards()\nwhen the disk moved" 760,480 260x80

# ── data ──
@ arrow file -> parse "text"
@ arrow parse -> merge_r "the disk's Board"
@ arrow merge_r -> canvas "merged Board"
@ arrow canvas -> merge_w "the canvas's Board"
@ arrow merge_w -> serialize "merged Board"
@ arrow serialize -> swap "text"
@ arrow swap -> file "the whole file at once"

# ── evidence ──
@ note evidence 0,840 """
code:
the two paths in the app and the merge they share
  @grafli/app.py:1367 _on_file_changed
  @grafli/app.py:1346 _reconcile_external
  @grafli/app.py:1155 _write_file
  @grafli/sync.py:216 merge_boards
  @grafli/sync.py:43 atomic_write
""" ~small
